Creating a Sierpinski Triangle in XAML can be a bit complex due to the recursive nature of the fractal, but it can be achieved using a combination of XAML and C# code-behind. Below is a step-by-step guide to creating a Sierpinski Triangle in a WPF application.

### Step 1: Set Up the WPF Project
1. Open Visual Studio.
2. Create a new WPF App (.NET Core) project.
3. Name your project and click "Create".

### Step 2: Add XAML for the Main Window
Open `MainWindow.xaml` and set up the basic structure.

```xml
